# Execution Graph & Dependency Analysis

Spec: ExecutionPlan
Purpose:
  Detailed execution graph schema — how tasks relate, how parallelism
  is determined, how critical path is calculated, how agents are assigned,
  and how crash recovery works via execution journal and checkpoints.

Owns: plans/execution-plan.sdd

## Dependency Graph

  Tasks are nodes; edges define dependencies:
    T100 → T103 (T103 depends on T100)
    T101 → T103
    T102 → T103

  AI reads graph, NOT task IDs, to determine execution order.

Example Graph:
  T100 (Domain)
  T101 (Repository)
  T102 (Provider)
    ↓  (all feed into T103)
  T103 (Refund Service)
    ↓
  T104 (API)    T105 (Tests)
    ↓              ↓
    T106 (Review) ←┘

## Sequential vs Parallel

  Tasks without dependency edges between them run in PARALLEL.
  Supervisor assigns to available agents based on:
    - task requirements (domain, level, skills)
    - agent capabilities
    - agent availability and load
    - resource locks
    - risk level

## Critical Path

  Longest dependency chain in the graph.
  Example: T100 → T103 → T104 → T106

  Used for bottleneck identification and project duration estimation.

## Parallel Capacity

  Supervisor monitors:
    READY: T100, T101, T102
    → Agent A → T100
    → Agent B → T101
    → Agent C → T102

## Task Risk Levels

  LOW       → auto execution
  MEDIUM    → agent + verification
  HIGH      → implementation + independent review
  CRITICAL  → human approval required

## Task Capability Matching

  T102 requires: Go, HTTP, Payment Provider, security
  Agent A: Go ✓, HTTP ✓, Payment ✓
  Agent B: Go ✓, HTTP ✓
  Agent C: security ✓

  → Agent A selected (best match)

## Execution Checkpoint

  For large tasks:
    CP1: architecture complete
    CP2: domain complete
    CP3: integration complete
    CP4: tests complete

## Crash Recovery

  If agent dies mid-task at 50%:
    last_checkpoint: CP2
    changes: recorded
    proof: pending

  New agent: resume T103 from CP2

## Execution Journal

  Each task has:
    @task.T103
    journal:
      started
      files_changed
      commands_run
      tests_run
      discoveries
      blockers
      decisions
      checkpoint

  Enables agent handoff without loss of context.

## Plan Repair

  When missing dependency detected (e.g., @skill.idempotency missing):
    INSERT research task: T110 (Research idempotency pattern)
    INSERT creation task: T111 (Create project skill)
    INSERT T103 after T110, T111

  This is plan evolution, not plan corruption.

